 and Emergencies\nLanding page: Getting Started at TU Berlin\nStrategy\nTU Berlin International 2030\nAnnual Reports\nPartnerships\nInternational Delegations\nNetworks\nStrategic Partnerships\nInternational partners\nGlobal Responsibility\nSupport for Ukraine\nGlobal South\nScholars at Risk\nProjects\nForo Acad\u00e9mico Chile-Alemania\nENHANCE\nGlobal Centre G-WAC\nGlobal Centre TRAJECTS\nFIT\nQuality and Innovation Offensive (QIO)\nVORsprung\nInternationalization@home\nInternationalization of administration\nInternational Insights\nInternational Day\nInternational Day 2025\nStrategy\nAbout Us\nYou are here:\nDepartment of International Affairs\nGetting Started at TU Berlin\nServices and Offers\nRecognition & Equivalence\nRecognition & Equivalence\nOur Recognition Office is your point of contact, whether you studied abroad and need help having your foreign credits recognized, are an international applicant and need your degrees recognized, or are an international student with a degree from TU Berlin and now need a certificate of equivalence.\nWe are here to help!\nRecognition & Equivalence\nRecognition of international credits\nCertificates of equivalence for TU degrees\nDoctoral studies with an international university degree\nRecognition & Equivalence\nThe Recognition Office is responsible for:\nRecognition of international credits and university degrees\nGuidance on pursuing doctoral studies with an international university degree\nCertificates of equivalence for TU degrees\nFor further questions about studying at TU Berlin please turn to the academic advising service.\nAdvising for international degree seeking students is available here.\nFor questions concerning admission and enrollment for international bachelor students please turn to the Servicebereich Bachelor or if you are an international master student to the Servicebereich Master.\nContact\nPeter Marock\nEquivalence / Deputy Head of Section\npeter.marock(at)tu-berlin.de\n+49 30 314-24692\n+49 30 314-24067\nOffice\nINT SB\nRoom\nH 0053\nAdvising hours\nTue 9:30 - 12:30 (via telephone) / Thur 9.30 - 12.30 (via telephone)\nQuick Links\nTU Berlin Academic Advising\nUndergraduate Admissions\nGraduate Admissions\nCenter for Junior Scholars (doctoral studies)\nRecognition of international credits\nExchange students who take part in university partnerships (ERAMSUS, overseas) can directly contact their relevant examination board after receiving their transcript of records (subject and grade list). Responsibility for the conversion of grades and credits lies with the respective examination board or module supervisor.\nYou can also refer to our grade conversion table for European exchange programs and the grade conversion table for overseas exchange programs.\nIf you are applying for a bachelor\u2019s program, please read the applicant information provided by Team Bachelor International.\nMaster\u2019s applicants can find information about statements of comparability at www.anabin.de\nIf you are applying for a higher degree semester in a master\u2019s program, please contact the relevant advisor for studies and teaching.\nYou can find all the forms you need here:\nThe application form for recognition of previously obtained credits is available here\nYou can find the contacts to the examination boards through the website of the particular study programs which are listed here.\nGrade Conversion Information\nGrade conversion Europe\n(pdf, 266 kB)\nGrade conversion Overseas\n(pdf, 305 kB)\nRecognition Information\n(pdf, 1.65 MB)\nRecognition Study\n(pdf, 896 kB)\nCertificates of equivalence for TU degrees\nOur office is happy to provide the following certificates of equivalence upon presentation of your original TU Berlin degree certificate:\nDiplomvorpr\u00fcfung/Magisterzwischenpr\u00fcfung\n(If you have also earned credits for at least 2 semesters of the Hauptstudium)\nBachelor\u2019s degree (English)\nLicence (French)\nDiplomhauptpr\u00fcfung/Magisterpr\u00fcfung:\nMaster\u2019s degree (English)\nDipl\u00f4me d'Etudes Approfondies (D.E.A.) / Master 2 \u2013 option recherche (French)\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\nDoctorate:\nPh.D. (English)\nDoctorat (French)\nDoctoral studies with an international university degree\nBefore you start your doctoral studies, you should inquire whether your final degree fulfills the admission requirements for doctoral studies in Germany or whether you have to complete additional studies before you can be admitted.\nThe Recognition Office can provide basic information about this.\nPlease email copies of your degree certificates and transcripts to peter.marock@tu-berlin.de.\nFirst steps for a doctoral procedure can be found here\nInformation on application and enrollment is available here\nCenter for Junior Scholars (CJS)\nAdvising from the CJS\nWe\u2019ve got the brains for the future.\nFor the benefit of society.\nContact\nSite Credits\nData Protection\nAccessibility\nCertificates\nAlumni\nPress\nhttps://www.tu.berlin/en/go28637/", "links": [["", "https://www.tu.berlin/en/"], ["Easy Read", "https://www.tu.berlin/en/footer/accessibility/easy-read-version"], ["Login", "https://www.tu.berlin/Shibboleth.sso/Login?target=%2Flogin-endpoint%3Flogintype%3Dlogin%26redirect_url%3Dhttps%253A%252F%252Ftuport.sap.tu-berlin.de%252F%26cHash%3Dc8bde08623cd285fc932773f3c4da225"], ["TU Portal", "https://tuport.sap.tu-berlin.de/"], ["Webmail", "https://webmail.tu-berlin.de/"], ["Intranet", "https://intranet.tu-berlin.de/"], ["Faculty I - Humanities and Educational Sciences", "https://www.tu.berlin/en/humanities"], ["Faculty II \u2013 Mathematics and Natural Sciences", "https://www.tu.berlin/en/naturwissenschaften"], ["Faculty III \u2013 Process Sciences", "https://www.tu.berlin/en/fakultaet3"], ["Faculty IV \u2013 Electrical Engineering and Computer Science", "https://www.tu.berlin/en/eecs"], ["Faculty V \u2013 Mechanical Engineering and Transport Systems", "https://www.tu.berlin/en/vm"], ["Faculty VI \u2013 P